      "side": 0,
      "message": "It seems the base debian10 image doesn\u0027t have clang and the build script currently really wants to build with clang (CXX\u003d/usr/local/bin/clang++). If there is a clang-debian10 that might work, or just installing clang as a package might work, though it\u0027s really old (looks like Debian10 came with Clang7, which is even older than the Clang8 in the google/clang-debian9). It looks like one can get to Clang11 with buster-backports, but I\u0027m not sure if that\u0027s how we want to get it.\n\nI always end up getting my clang from Chromium with https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:tools/clang/scripts/update.py (directions for use at top of file).",
      "range": {
